**The problem**:
```java
@Service  // singleton
public class TaskService {
    @Autowired
    private TaskProcessor processor; // prototype — but only created ONCE!
    // All uses share the SAME processor instance
}
```

**Solutions**:
1. **`ObjectProvider<T>`** — call `getObject()` each time you need a fresh instance
2. **`ApplicationContext.getBean()`** — but this is Service Locator (anti-pattern)
3. **`@Lookup` method injection** — Spring overrides the method to return a new prototype

```java
@Service
public class TaskService {
    @Autowired
    private ObjectProvider<TaskProcessor> processorProvider;

    public void processTask(Task task) {
        TaskProcessor processor = processorProvider.getObject(); // NEW each time
        processor.execute(task);
    }
}
```
